# PDS Storefront

- `packages/storefront` is the Next.js documentation site and should model best-practice use of PDS components.
- Prefer `@porsche-design-system/components-react/ssr` for UI primitives in app code and examples.
- Keep MDX and docs content accessible: meaningful link text, correct heading order, appropriate image `alt` text, and keyboard-usable examples.
- Avoid custom clickable `div`/`span` patterns when a PDS component or native semantic element fits.
- If a change affects interactive UI, consider the matching validation surface: `npm run test:unit:storefront`, `npm run test:e2e:storefront`, `npm run test:a11y:storefront`, and `npm run test:vrt:storefront`.
- Files in `public/assets/downloads/` are downloadable templates; keep them aligned with active repo guidance instead of treating them as source code behavior.
